  "production_changes": [
    "Transport desired state is separate from server-confirmed bars/quotes/trades. Only supplied valid channel lists confirm current generation; omitted channels are untouched. Explicit empty clears channel. Successful send alone never establishes completion.",
    "Serialized subscription changes wait at most2s including send/ACK, with5s minimum retry cadence per operation/channel. Partial responses, provider errors, malformed channels, lost ACK, cancellation and stale generations stay incomplete. Desired subscriptions remain available for retry/reconnect.",
    "Current-generation reader starts before resubscription waits. Unexpected graceful/exceptional closure revokes state and uses bounded reconnect attempts/backoff. Deliberate disconnect cancels owned tasks and revokes intent; late authentication/messages cannot restore stale state.",
    "Provider retains configured startup failure and retries via existing per-tick subscription sync on30s cadence. Whole startup including history has25s timeout, additionally subject to existing engine5s sync deadline. Scheduler retains degraded configured provider so entries remain blocked rather than falling back to provider=None.",
    "Historical prefill keeps feature history but cannot seed receipt freshness. New connection generation clears prior live receipts; an advancing fresh bar is required. Existing duplicate/future/out-of-order/stale-bar and all entry/exit thresholds remain intact.",
    "Unsubscribe requires explicit all-channel confirmation before provider buffers and membership retire. Status includes exact subscription completeness; fresh SPY cannot hide unconfirmed NEW, and unknown age is null rather than0.",
    "Startup retries skip historical prefill inside the shorter sync deadline, retaining configured client and normal feeder history fallback. Initial startup prefill remains unchanged; neither history path establishes live freshness."
  ],
